+# Retail explosion transient-light run (2026-10-20)
+
+Two Release runs used the same active NAP snapshot, QA mission, display, 1280x720 resolution, and dynamic-light setting. Both used `--invulnerable=on`. The only renderer option changed was `--render-transient-effect-lights=on|off`.
+
+Both runs reached `FP7_system`, spawned the test ship, executed `fp7_base_explode`, and ran `qa_destroy_test_fighter_explosion`. Neither log contains a renderer exception. Existing THN `StartIK` warnings are unrelated to this lighting check.
+
+## Retail asset provenance
+
+The active effects package was not replaced with a QA light curve. Rebuilding it from
+`Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/explosion-ship-qa-20261018-retail-inputs/Effects`
+produced the exact active archive SHA-256
+`e74d528a81e0fe628b545020fd5513a72bb07bcb1314aa653eee8e7b39ab0415`.
+The rebuilt archive passed verification for all 661 entries. The retail
+`elite_flash_to_red` light animation and explosion definitions remain unchanged.
+
+The M01A mission package was built from files under `Data/NAP/`. Its only
+difference from the source mission tree is `missions/m01a/M01a.ini`, which
+adds a reproducible test-ship spawn and destroy trigger. It does not alter
+effects or lighting data. The captured active manifest is included here.
+
+## Captures
+
+| Transient effect lights on | Transient effect lights off |
+|---|---|
+| ![Retail explosion with transient lighting enabled](frame-on.png) | ![Retail explosion with transient lighting disabled](frame-off.png) |
+
+The frames are selected around each destruction trigger, but camera position
+and animation phase are not pixel-aligned. The explosion particles remain
+visible with the option off, as expected for emissive effects. These captures
+confirm that the retail explosion path runs under both settings; they do not
+calibrate the light's visual contribution. The side-by-side image and complete
+logs are included. Full-rate captures and test staging remain under
+`Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/renderer-retail-effect-light-20261020/`.
+
+## Reproduction and verification
+
+Run from the staged app directory after verifying `active.json`:
+
+```text
+lancer client-retail-lights-on.ini --new-game --invulnerable=on --render-dynamic-lighting=on --render-transient-effect-lights=on
+lancer client-retail-lights-off.ini --new-game --invulnerable=on --render-dynamic-lighting=on --render-transient-effect-lights=off
+```
+
+The focused runtime log paths are [on](runtime-on.log) and [off](runtime-off.log).
+`nexus-pack verify-active` passed for the captured manifest. The application
+root had no loose `DATA`/ `data` directories or package symlinks.
